# MasterWork locale file — en-US
# Format: Key=Value  (one string per line)
#
# Hand-authored setup + scoring passage strings for my-fathers-work-template. These are the
# template's own keys — the setup/scoring passages used to borrow keys from cost-of-disease's
# extracted restext (TCOD_TownName_*, PlayerNameIntro_*, NameEntryTownConfirm_*, Number_*_Lower),
# which was never appropriate for shared template content. Copy this file alongside the
# passages/layouts when integrating the template into a real module (see
# scripts/apply-template.ps1) — a target module's own extracted en-US.restext is a separate file
# and these keys are namespaced (Setup_/Scoring_/Common_/Countdown_) to avoid colliding with it.
#
# Countdown_* backs the countdown_action popup's own digit/REVEAL text (Showcase_Popup_
# RevealCountdown.mws.yaml) — these are displayed via CSS-timed opacity, not markdown/template
# substitution, but the display strings themselves still need to be real restext, not literal CSS
# `content` values, so they're actually localizable. The real extractor should synthesize
# equivalent keys the same way it does for SpecialEvent_Title (ViewSpecialEvent has no Cradle
# text() call for its own overlay text either — this is app-side UI text, not story content, in
# both cases).

Common_Close=Close
Common_Continue=Continue

Setup_PlayerCount_Title=Players
Setup_PlayerCount_Prompt=How many individuals will be sharing this experience today?
Setup_PlayerCount_Two=2 Players
Setup_PlayerCount_Three=3 Players
Setup_PlayerCount_Four=4 Players

Setup_Number_Two=two
Setup_Number_Three=three
Setup_Number_Four=four

Setup_PlayerIntro_Body1=As siblings of an influential family of Eastern European descent, the **{playtxt}** of us have received a not-insignificant portion of our family's estate.
Setup_PlayerIntro_Body2=Before we begin, let us make this historical fiction more engaging by providing our names.

Setup_PassBook_A=Carefully pass the storybook to Player A
Setup_PassBook_B=Carefully pass the storybook to Player B
Setup_PassBook_C=Carefully pass the storybook to Player C
Setup_PassBook_D=Carefully pass the storybook to Player D

Setup_NameEntry_LabelA=Player A - Please enter your given name:
Setup_NameEntry_LabelB=Player B - Please enter your given name:
Setup_NameEntry_LabelC=Player C - Please enter your given name:
Setup_NameEntry_LabelD=Player D - Please enter your given name:

Setup_Greeting_1=Welcome to My Father's Work,
Setup_Greeting_2=Greetings and welcome to My Father's Work,
Setup_Greeting_3=We are delighted to receive you,
Setup_Greeting_4=Welcome, dear sibling,
Setup_WarmRegards=Our warmest regards.

Setup_TownName_Title=The Village
Setup_TownName_Intro=Now that our given names have been established, we must also search our recollection for the name of the village which our vast estates overlook. Considering the myriad of small towns in the Hungarian countryside, it would be unmeritably forward to not allow the group a chance to collectively name the place they will now inhabit.
Setup_TownName_InputLabel=Please collectively enter the name of the town in which your inheritance resides.
Setup_TownName_ConfirmBody1=Thank you and please do excuse our forgetfulness.
Setup_TownName_ConfirmBody2=Of course, {townname} is an appropriate and fitting moniker for a place to conduct important scientific research. In fact, history will remember this name, mark my words.

Setup_NarrationVoice_Title=Narrator's Voice
Setup_NarrationVoice_Prompt=Before we proceed, might we trouble you to select a voice for our narrator?
Setup_NarrationVoice_Male=A Gentleman's Voice
Setup_NarrationVoice_Female=A Lady's Voice

Scoring_Entry_Title=Score Entry
Scoring_Header_Player=Player
Scoring_Entry_HeaderScore=Score
Scoring_HelpBody=Add any additional points from Vanity Estate Upgrades

Scoring_TieBreaker_Title=Tie Breaker
Scoring_TieBreaker1_Subtitle=Masterwork Completed
Scoring_TieBreaker1_HeaderCompleted=Completed Masterwork
Scoring_TieBreaker2_Subtitle=Estate Upgrades
Scoring_TieBreaker2_HeaderUpgrades=Estate Upgrades

Scoring_Rank_Title=Rankings
Scoring_Rank_1st=1st
Scoring_Rank_2nd=2nd
